# Global Execution & Workflow Rules

## 1. Memory Bank & Context Protocol (Pointers Over Payloads)
- **Primary Goal is Execution:** Your priority is writing code, generating schemas, or delegating tasks. Do not get stuck in a documentation loop.
- **Single Update Rule:** Update `memory/activeContext.md` and `memory/progress.md` EXACTLY ONCE per task—only at the very end, immediately before calling `attempt_completion` or `new_task`.
- **Pointers Over Payloads (Strict Token Limit):** Keep memory files aggressively concise to save context tokens. NEVER copy-paste code blocks, raw Figma AST data, CSS values, or full JSON/YAML schemas into `.md` files. Log ONLY URLs, specific node IDs, file paths, and high-level bullet points.
- **Mandatory Reads:** At the start of EVERY task, read `memory/activeContext.md` AND `memory/projectBrief.md`.
- **Read Before Asking (Zero-Punting):** Before asking the user for specifications, check memory files and audits first. Do not punt questions to the user if the data is already in your workspace.

## 2. Component-Driven CMS Architecture (Kentico)
- **Separation of Concerns:** Keep content/data files separate from structural layout templates.
- **Templates (`content/templates/*.yaml`):** Define structural skeletons ONLY. Keys limited to `slug`, `title`, and `sections`. NEVER add text copy here.
- **Pages (`content/pages/*.yaml`):** The data source of truth. Contains structured copy and variant parameters.
- **No Raw HTML in Data:** Never embed raw HTML blocks or inline styling directly inside YAML.

## 3. Style Modernization & Legacy Retirement
- **SCSS Source of Truth:** Write and edit styling exclusively in modular SCSS (`dev/assets/css/scss/`).
- **Read-Only Files:** Never hand-edit compiled outputs (`dist/`, `previews/`, `*.min.css`) or legacy CSS files (`dev/assets/css/legacy/`).

## 4. Strict Port Configuration & Isolation
- **User Preview Port (4000):** All local development servers intended for user viewing run strictly on Port 4000.
- **Agent/Testing Port (4001):** All automated audits, Puppeteer scripts, static preview servers, and background HTTP tasks run strictly on Port 4001.
- **URL Target Verification:** Any script targeting `localhost` or `127.0.0.1` must point to `http://localhost:4001`. Never use Port 3000, 3001, or 3003.

## 5. Canonical Project Constants
- **Figma File Key:** ALWAYS use `80i51JCUKVIrTZ8Zt9y73X` for all Figma MCP tool calls. Never search for, guess, or attempt to use any other Figma file key string.

## 6. Action-First Tool Execution
- Always execute file modifications (`write_file`, `replace_in_file`) or terminal tools immediately without conversational preambles.
- Chain multi-step terminal verifications into a single invocation using `&&`. Do not re-run a silent successful command.

## 7. Holistic Validation (Content, Styles, Functionality)
- **Content:** Every text node, label, and input placeholder must strictly match the Figma AST data extraction.
- **Styles:** CSS tokens (typography, padding, box-shadow, colors) must match Figma node values 1:1.
- **Functionality:** Invisible reCAPTCHA v3 must be properly configured, buttons must be single-source CTAs for forms, and input fields must be functionally accessible.

## 8. Asset & Placehold.co Guardrails
- **Placehold.co Enforcement:** If a Figma image URL is missing or a `/getmedia/` local path is broken, you MUST inject `https://placehold.co/[width]x[height]` matching the exact bounding box dimensions extracted from Figma.
- **Asset Bounds Guard:** Headless tests must confirm image bounding boxes (`getBoundingClientRect()`) evaluate to non-zero width and height.

## 9. Fluid Responsive & Tablet Testing
- **Tablet Consideration:** You must account for tablet layouts. Hardcoded desktop widths that crush on 768px screens are unacceptable. Layouts must be fluid.
- **Tri-Viewport Protocol:** `window.getComputedStyle()` audits must be tested across Desktop (1440px), Tablet (768px), and Mobile (375px) on Port 4001.

## 10. Autonomous Ping-Pong & Handoff Loop (No User Escalation)
- **Never Escalate on First Failure:** If a build fails, a schema validation fails, or a Puppeteer audit fails, YOU MUST NOT stop and ask the user for help. You must autonomously analyze the error, rewrite the code, and re-test up to 3 times.
- **The QA-Gatekeeper Loop:** `frontend-dev` is strictly forbidden from declaring a task complete to the user. Once `frontend-dev` passes local tests, it MUST invoke `new_task` to hand off to `qa-runner`. 
- **QA Rejection:** If `qa-runner` detects a defect, it MUST NOT alert the user. It must invoke `new_task` to send the failure log back to `frontend-dev` for immediate remediation. The user is only notified upon 100% QA success.

## 11. Structural DOM Assertions (Pre-CSS Math)
- **Structure Before Paint:** Before measuring CSS computed styles, the agent MUST programmatically verify the DOM tree hierarchy.
- **Verification Requirements:** Assert that flex/grid columns do not collapse, that text and forms are in separate isolated columns, and checklists render correctly. If the HTML tree is wrong, do not proceed to CSS validation.

## 12. Anti-False-Positive Testing
- **Figma-Sourced Assertions:** Audit scripts must explicitly define expected values by extracting them directly from the Figma MCP payload. Do not hardcode expected values based on your own CSS output. Assert `Live_DOM_Value === Figma_AST_Value`.
- **Structural Hierarchy Anti-Hallucination:** Never assume structural compliance based on isolated CSS properties. If structural disconnects occur, print the generated HTML fragment directly to the console for inspection.

## 13. The "Figma First" Styling Protocol
- **No Blind CSS:** You must NEVER write SCSS, CSS, or inline styles without first querying the live Figma MCP for the specific Node ID. Do not guess padding, margins, colors, or dimensions.
- **Schema Over Hacks:** If CSS `!important` tags fail to achieve visual parity, STOP writing CSS. Update the YAML schema (`content/pages/*.yaml`) and the HTML Template Engine (`dev/scripts/build-cms-inline.mjs`) to generate explicit semantic HTML wrappers before applying styles.

## 14. Static Asset Serving Guard
- Before executing Puppeteer DOM evaluations on Port 4001, verify that the static HTTP server is correctly serving BOTH the HTML output directory AND its sibling `./css` directory. If CSS assets return 404, halt the audit and fix the server route first.

## 15. Flat Asset Bundling & Network Verification
- **No Directory Traversal:** Never use `../../` or `../` pathing for web assets. Local HTTP servers block path traversals above the web root.
- **Flat Bundling Protocol:** The build pipeline MUST physically copy all compiled CSS/JS assets into a sibling folder (e.g., `./css/`) within the final output directory. All generated HTML must link to these flat, localized assets.

## 16. Production CSS Baseline Protection
- **Read-Only Baselines:** Legacy stylesheets (e.g., `style-cms.css`) are strictly read-only.
- **Dedicated Override Layer:** New design tokens must be written to and compiled into `figma-overrides.css`, injected into the HTML `<head>` directly *after* the read-only baseline.

## 17. Figma MCP Depth & Node Bounds Safety
- **Forbidden Root Queries:** NEVER call `get_figma_data` with only a `fileKey`. You MUST explicitly pass both `fileKey` AND a specific `nodeId` (e.g., `nodeId: "296:63"`).
- **Depth Constraints:** Always set a strict `depth` limit (maximum `depth: 3`) on Figma MCP queries to prevent payload token explosions.

## 18. Silent Headless Browser Execution & Tool Bans
- **Strict Tool Ban:** You are strictly forbidden from using the built-in `browser_action` tool. All browser inspections must occur silently via the Puppeteer MCP server with `--headless=new` arguments on Port 4001.

## 19. Hard Failure on MCP Tool Errors
- **No Silent Memory Fallbacks:** If an MCP tool (such as Figma MCP) returns an error, you MUST NOT fall back to local memory files or guess. Halt execution immediately, state the exact MCP error, and wait for user intervention.

## 20. Configuration Validation Rules
- **Port Conflict Detection:** Before executing any server process, verify that the target port (4000 or 4001) is not already in use. Use `lsof -i :PORT` to check availability.
- **Model Consistency Audit:** All agent mode definitions in `.roomodes` must reference `anthropic/claude-sonnet-4` or approved cost-efficient alternatives. Mismatches trigger immediate correction.
- **Figma File Key Validation:** Every Figma MCP call MUST include the canonical key `80i51JCUKVIrTZ8Zt9y73X`. Calls without explicit nodeId are forbidden.

## 21. Cross-Agent State Tracking Protocols
- **Handoff Checkpoints:** Before invoking `new_task`, the current agent MUST write a concise checkpoint to `memory/activeContext.md` containing: (1) completed steps, (2) exact file paths modified, (3) next agent's required inputs, (4) any blocking issues.
- **Rejection Loop Tracking:** If `qa-runner` rejects a build, it MUST record the exact failure (line number, assertion, computed vs. expected value) in `memory/activeContext.md` before handing back to `frontend-dev`.
- **Data Mapper Halt Protocol:** If `data-mapper` encounters a structural HTML requirement, it MUST halt immediately and invoke `new_task` in `frontend-dev` mode with the exact YAML path and required change.

## 22. Memory System Enhancement & Workflow Checkpoints
- **Structured Checkpoints:** Memory files MUST track: (1) Phase name, (2) Agent responsible, (3) Completion status (✅/❌), (4) Critical file paths, (5) Next handoff target.
- **Validation Gate Definitions:** Each agent handoff MUST include explicit validation criteria (e.g., "DOM math passes on 1440px, 768px, 375px" or "Zero schema violations").
- **Token Efficiency:** Keep all memory entries under 5 lines per checkpoint. Use abbreviations (e.g., "DOM math ✅" instead of "Computed DOM mathematics validation passed").

## 23. Build Pipeline Integrity
- **Chained Verification:** All build commands MUST be chained with `&&` to ensure sequential execution and immediate failure detection.
- **Exit Code Assertion:** Every build step MUST explicitly verify exit code 0. Non-zero exits trigger autonomous retry (up to 3 attempts) before escalation.
- **Asset Availability Guard:** Before serving on Port 4001, verify that CSS, JS, and image assets are physically present in the output directory and accessible via HTTP GET.

## 24. Autonomous Retry & Recovery Protocol
- **Three-Strike Rule:** If a build, schema validation, or Puppeteer audit fails, the responsible agent MUST autonomously retry up to 3 times with incremental fixes before requesting user intervention.
- **Failure Logging:** Each retry MUST log the exact error, attempted fix, and result to `memory/activeContext.md` for audit trail.
- **Silent Recovery:** Retries MUST NOT alert the user. Only final success or unrecoverable errors trigger user notification.
|
## 25. Mandatory Architect Review Protocol
- **Mandatory Architect Review:** At task completion, `kentico-architect` MUST review and update if necessary: `README.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `.clinerules`, `.roomodes`, `.rooignore`, `.gitignore`.
- **No Screenshot Images:** All agents are forbidden from creating screenshot images. Use headless Puppeteer console output only.
- **Documentation Protocol:** No additional `.md` files unless explicitly instructed by the user. Agent-created documentation must be placed under `docs/` directory only.

## 26. Agent File Editing Restrictions (Enforceable)

### kentico-architect
- **Editable:** `memory/activeContext.md`, `memory/projectBrief.md` (pointers only)
- **Forbidden:** All implementation files. Read-only advisor role. Use `new_task` to delegate.

### frontend-dev
- **Editable:** `content/pages/`, `content/templates/`, `dev/`, `docs/`, `memory/activeContext.md`, `memory/progress.md`, `memory/projectBrief.md`, `.clinerules`, `.gitignore`, `.rooignore`, `package.json`, `README.md`
- **Forbidden:** `.roomodes`, `AGENTS.md` (read-only), `dev/scripts/*.mjs` (build scripts read-only)

### data-mapper
- **Editable:** `content/pages/`, `content/templates/`, `docs/`, `memory/activeContext.md`, `memory/progress.md`
- **Forbidden:** `dev/`, `.mjs` files, `.clinerules`, `.roomodes`, `AGENTS.md`, `package.json`

### qa-runner
- **Editable:** `dev/`, `docs/`, `memory/activeContext.md`, `memory/progress.md`, `package.json`
- **Forbidden:** `content/`, `.clinerules`, `.roomodes`, `AGENTS.md`, `README.md`

### Enforcement Protocol
- File restriction errors MUST be thrown immediately on attempted edit
- Error message MUST include: agent name, attempted file path, allowed file patterns
- No silent failures or fallback mechanisms
